course: dictionary
lesson: 15442
title: Stealth: moving unseen
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stealth means moving or acting quietly and secretly, so that no one notices you. Look at the words around it for clues. «The cat crept across the room with stealth, so the mouse never saw it coming.» Crept and never saw it coming tell you the cat was quiet and secret.
explain: «The spy opened the locked door by stealth.» By stealth means the spy did it in secret, without anyone knowing. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The spy opened the locked door secretly" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: Stealth is also used in games and machines. «Stealth mode» means sneaking past enemies instead of fighting them. A «stealth bomber» is a plane that is hard to spot on radar. The idea is the same each time: hard to notice.
fact: Stealth means moving or acting quietly and secretly so that no one notices you.
fact: «By stealth» and «with stealth» both mean doing something secretly.
fact: Stealth can be a noun, as in «the stealth of a cat», or it can come before a noun, as in «a stealth plane».
fact: Stealth technology makes planes, ships or other machines hard to detect by radar.
fact: In video games, stealth means sneaking past enemies instead of fighting them.
exercise: «The cat moved with stealth across the garden.» What does stealth mean here? | Running as fast as it can | Sleeping in the sun | *Moving quietly so no one notices | Making a loud noise
exercise: In a video game, what does «stealth mode» mean? | Fighting every enemy head on | *Sneaking past enemies instead of fighting | Stopping the game to rest | Making the screen brighter
exercise: «The stealth bomber flew over the city without being seen on radar.» What does stealth suggest about the plane? | It is made of wood | *It is hard to detect | It is painted bright red | It is very slow
test: Which word is closest in meaning to stealth? | Anger | *Secrecy | Noise | Speed
test: «The cat hunted the mouse by stealth.» Was the cat loud or quiet? | Loud | Angry | *Quiet and secret | Lost
exam: Which sentence uses stealth correctly? | The stealth sun rose over the hill | *The fox approached the chickens with stealth so they did not hear it | He ate his stealth lunch in the cafe | The band played with stealth at full volume
